;; THE SET THE KIT WRITES INTO A PROJECT: the project's whole toolchain, which the KIT owns (the
;; person, 2026-10-28: "KIT owns whole tools set"). `bb init` and `bb upgrade` write it into the
;; application, over what the pinned template generated, as a commit of their own
;; (`harness.setup.project-set`); the template's own numbers are placeholders the KIT overwrites.
;; Hand-written, and the one place each value is written: `bb health` builds the generated
;; application's image from it, and `bb health --record` copies the set it proved into
;; `known-good.edn` as `:project` (plan 7.0, item 7.4).
;;
;;   :tools         every line under `.mise.toml`'s [tools], by mise's name for the tool. The
;;                  values are the ones the KIT's own gates run (`known-good.edn`). java: mise
;;                  runs exactly the version a file names (it takes no range for java), so this is
;;                  the project's default, not a floor - 21 and newer works, and an adopter on 21
;;                  says so in a gitignored `.mise.local.toml`, which mise reads over the file
;;   :build-image   the Dockerfile's build stage: Temurin 25 with the Clojure CLI of :tools
;;   :runtime-image the Dockerfile's runtime stage: Docker Hub's newest Temurin 25 JRE on Alpine
;;
;; The Dockerfile's `BB_VERSION` and `TAILWIND_VERSION` are written from :tools as well.

{:tools {:java "temurin-25"
         :clojure "1.12.6.1673"
         :babashka "1.13.226"
         :clj-kondo "2026.08.04"
         :cljfmt "0.16.6"
         :tailwindcss "4.3.3"}
 :build-image "clojure:temurin-25-tools-deps-1.12.6.1673-alpine"
 :runtime-image "eclipse-temurin:25.0.4.1_1-jre-alpine"}
